From 5044f38831bf64918a3992843fa1552467d48588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 11:13:17 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Mac: tab groups in the unified strip

The tab menu's group items work now. A group belongs to the window of its
profile, and its tabs stay together in the unified strip: a header chip
in the group's color before them and a line in that color along them
(rows indented with the line at their edge with vertical tabs, a dot
when the column is collapsed). Clicking the header collapses or expands
the group, right-clicking it opens Chromium's group editor there; a new
group from the tab menu opens it too.

Dragging a tab between the tabs of a group of its profile adds it to
the group, dragging it out removes it; groups of other profiles are
jumped over. Dragging a header moves the whole group between other
groups. Ctrl+Tab skips the tabs of collapsed groups, and the move-tab
keys join, leave or jump over groups like Chromium's.
